review:
New York Mysteries has made a lot of improvement since Secrets of the Mafia. Now the story is more engaging, the cutscenes look clearer, the mystery keeps you playing until the end, you get to play with two characters (one in the main game and the other in the bonus chapter) and, for the first time since I began playing this type of game, I got all the collectibles!

PROS:
- Amazing graphics;
- Engaging story;
- Clearer cutscenes;
- Female (main game) and male (bonus chapter) characters gameplay;
- Easy to read journal;
- Fast travelling map;
- Different style of HO minigames (you don't have to find an irrevelant list of objects);
- The Map contains images of locations with certain icons that show if the player has taken the collectibles or not, it comes pretty handy;
- American history collectibles is the most appreciated item in the game!! (Thank you, developers!)

NEUTRE:
- I would have wanted to play as the Reaper. :)

CONS:
- When zooming in on an object with a plus symbol (that needs another object to become of use in the game), you don't get an "X" to get out of the zoom in. You must click around the inventory bar to get out.
- No other disadvantages found.

New York Mysteries: The Lantern of the Souls is the game for you if you happen to love the 1920s American detective novels.
